      "refs": [
        "action:n1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin with,"
      ],
      "justification": "The opening temporal phrase implicitly starts the process (init). The 'start' action is redundant but restates the same initialization concept, so it is treated as a match per the redundancy rule."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "choose your destination and calculate the distance"
      ],
      "justification": "Direct extraction of the first explicit process step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "continue to check if you need to book a train or a flight"
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully captures the concurrent/parallel check described in the text."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the answer is \"no\", then proceed to book a train. However, if the answer is \"yes\", then book a flight."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional phrasing implies the XOR decision point. Its two opposing outcomes map directly to the 'book a train' and 'book a flight' action nodes."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If a code is available within 24 hours"
      ],
      "justification": "The condition establishes the verification step and implicitly creates the decision gateway for the train path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "the process will end"
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly describes the positive outcome state and the terminal node for this branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "you should call a travel agency"
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the fallback action when the time threshold is exceeded."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, if 24 hours have passed, you should call a travel agency."
      ],
      "justification": "Calling the agency concludes this path. The explicit 'end of process' action is redundant with the structural end node but repeats the same termination logic, so it is matched."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "branch:b3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If a code is available",
        "On the other hand, if a code is not available"
      ],
      "justification": "The contrasting conditions for the flight path imply the exclusive choice gateway."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "the process will end along with the hotel reservation"
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps to the termination condition and associated cleanup step for the positive flight branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "the process will end as well"
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly signals process termination for the negative flight branch. The named action node is redundant with the structural end node but faithfully restates the same conclusion."
    }
